{"name":"State controlled-substance scheduling of xylazine and tianeptine","description":"For each US state that has acted, the controlled-substance schedule it assigns to substances that are NOT federally scheduled: xylazine and tianeptine — sourced from the state's own statute or administrative rule. Answers 'is tianeptine legal in [state]', 'is xylazine a controlled substance in [state]', and 'what schedule is tianeptine in [state]'. Control is entirely state-by-state, it is moving fast (states acted 2023–2026), and crucially the schedule is NOT the same everywhere: tianeptine is Schedule I in Florida, Georgia, Virginia, Minnesota, Delaware and Ohio but Schedule II in Tennessee, North Carolina and Nebraska, and xylazine is Schedule I in Florida, Schedule III in Delaware, Ohio, Nebraska and South Carolina, and Schedule IV in West Virginia. The only cross-state assemblies are a March-2024 PDF (LAPPA, xylazine only) and citation-free listicles. Kratom generally, 7-hydroxymitragynine (controlled federally by DEA temporary order from 2026, and at state level through kratom-product laws rather than schedules) and delta-8 are out of scope — seller sites cover them comprehensively. A state whose instrument cannot be confirmed on a fetched page is omitted, not guessed.","url":"https://referencesource.org/state-emerging-substance-scheduling/","licence":"unknown","last_verified":"2026-08-19","stale_after":"2027-02-15","sources":["https://delcode.delaware.gov/title16/c047/sc02/index.html","http://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0800-0899/0893/Sections/0893.03.html","https://codes.findlaw.com/ga/title-16-crimes-and-offenses/ga-code-sect-16-13-25.html","https://www.revisor.mn.gov/statutes/cite/152.02","https://nebraskalegislature.gov/laws/statutes.php?statute=28-405","https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_90/GS_90-90.html","https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-administrative-code/rule-4729:9-1-01","https://codes.fin